      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The curtain crashed down on another Toronto Maple Leafs season - a grim 32-36-14 slog that left them <strong>8th in the Atlantic, 31 points adrift and clutching the 15th overall draft slot</strong> after a humiliating seven-game skid to close it out. No playoffs for the first time in years, echoing the ghosts of 2016 when lottery gods smiled; this time, the ping-pong balls barely blinked, handing them a middling pick in a draft brimming with blue-chip forwards who could jolt this stagnant core. What went wrong? Goaltending crumbled like wet cardboard, the power play flatlined at historic futility, and that vaunted Big Four - Matthews, Marner, Nylander, Tavares - carried the load but couldn't drag the bottom-six or blueline out of the muck. Shanahan's regime stares down a reckoning: coaching purge? Dubas redux in the front office? Free agency looms with cap hell, but here's the silver lining - a top-15 selection offers a lifeline. Punchless summers breed desperate winters in Leafs Nation. <strong>Watch the lottery draw tonight; a miracle jump could rewrite this franchise's cursed draft narrative - or confirm it's 2016 all over again.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated May 13, 2026"
      },
